	<annotations>
		<text id="0" type="text/markdown" rect="(20, -150, 360, 50)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Lab 4: Regression Analysis**  
HDI dataset, 188 countries</text>
		<text id="1" type="text/markdown" rect="(360, 150, 190, 90)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 1: Explore**  
Load HDI with the Datasets widget and look at it.</text>
		<text id="2" type="text/markdown" rect="(60, 570, 330, 100)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Steps 1-2: Prepare**  
HDI set as the target, features normalized to [0, 1], then a 50% / 50% split into training and testing sets.</text>
		<text id="3" type="text/markdown" rect="(1540, 270, 320, 70)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 3: Linear regression**  
Three models (no regularization, Lasso, Elastic Net) scored with 10-fold cross-validation.</text>
		<text id="4" type="text/markdown" rect="(1200, 800, 230, 80)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 4: Coefficients**  
One table of coefficients for each model.</text>
		<text id="5" type="text/markdown" rect="(1200, 1000, 260, 100)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 5: Rank**  
Top 1 feature by RReliefF, then Elastic Net again on just that feature.</text>
		<text id="6" type="text/markdown" rect="(290, -170, 250, 90)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 6: Test data**  
Testing set connected so the models can be scored on test data.</text>
		<text id="7" type="text/markdown" rect="(1340, 1450, 290, 100)" font-family="Helvetica" font-size="14">**Step 7: Other models**  
AdaBoost, Random Forest, Neural Network and kNN, tuned for the lowest cross-validated RMSE.</text>
		<arrow id="8" start="(400, 240)" end="(330, 250)" fill="#C1272D" />
		<arrow id="9" start="(250, 570)" end="(275, 525)" fill="#1F77B4" />
